  "id": "miami",
  "intro": "Miami is the American gateway to the Caribbean and Latin America, and the radio shows it. Miami Center works oceanic traffic across the whole Caribbean basin, the cruise port is the largest in the world, and the marine band carries everything from container ships to a very large recreational fleet. West of the city the Everglades begin abruptly — a genuine wilderness with airboats, park service traffic and almost no cellular coverage, fifteen minutes from a major metro. Hurricane season shapes everything from June to November.",
  "introz": "迈阿密是美国通往加勒比和拉美的门户，无线电上看得很清楚。迈阿密区调管制整个加勒比海盆的越洋航班，邮轮港是全球最大的，海事频段上从集装箱船到极其庞大的休闲船队应有尽有。城西是骤然开始的大沼泽地——一片真正的荒野，有汽艇、公园管理局的通信，几乎没有手机信号，而这距离一个大都会区只有十五分钟。六月到十一月的飓风季决定着这里的一切。",
